      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:2:1:5",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) قَالَ أَبِي إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ لَيَصُومُ يَوْماً تَطَوُّعاً يُرِيدُ مَا عِنْدَ اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ فَيُدْخِلُهُ اللَّهُ بِهِ الْجَنَّةَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Shazaan, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya Bin Usman, from Ismail Bin Yasaar who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘My<sup>asws</sup> father<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The man who Fasts for one day voluntarily, intending what is in the Presence of Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic, so Allah<sup>azwj</sup> would Enter him into the Paradise due to it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Muhammad ibn Isma‘il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Uthman from Isma‘il ibn Yasar who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘My father has said, “When a person completes a day of optional fasting for the sake of Allah, the Most Majestic, the Most Glorious, Allah admits him in Paradise.’”” "
        ]
      }
    },
